# Route guides maintenance

Whenever you **implement or materially change** a page, section, or feature in `apps/web` or `apps/extension`, update the matching guide under **`docs/guides/routes/`** in the **same change**. The first UI phase (2) creates `docs/guides/routes/README.md` (index) and `docs/guides/_template.md`.

## Which file to update

Mirror the app URL (omit dynamic params), rooted at `docs/guides/routes/`. The index in `docs/guides/routes/README.md` is authoritative; do not keep a second route→file table here.

| Route pattern | Guide location |
| --- | --- |
| `/jobs`, `/jobs/:id` | `docs/guides/routes/jobs/index.md`, `detail.md` (dynamic params inline) |
| `/tracks/...` | `docs/guides/routes/tracks/...` |
| `/resume/...` | `docs/guides/routes/resume/...` |
| `/settings/...` | `docs/guides/routes/settings/...` |

## What to document

Per page/section: **behavior**, **save paths** (UI action → API endpoint → DB effect), **validation**, **RBAC** (which roles can view/edit), **agent parity** (equivalent MCP tool or CLI command? if not, why not), **edge cases**, **implementation map** (web + API paths), and **user-facing knowledge** (plain-language summary and common questions, no code or column names).

Update the **Progress overview** table when section status changes. Mark guide **Status** `Pending` → `Documented` when substantive.

## When guides need no change

Typos, internal renames with no behavior change, pure refactors that don't alter UX/API/validation.
